.\" Distro-authored man page for the Fedora pidp8i package.
.\" Candidate for upstreaming to the PiDP-8/I project.
.TH OS8-RUN 1 "November 21, 2026" "PiDP-8/I" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
os8-run \- run OS/8 boot scripts in the PDP-8 simulator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B os8-run
.RI [ \-h ]
.RI [ \-d ]
.RI [ \-v | \-vv ]
.RI [ \-\-enable " enable_option" ] ...
.RI [ \-\-disable " disable_option" ] ...
.I script
.RI [ script ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B os8-run
boots an OS/8 environment in the SIMH PDP-8 simulator and executes the
named boot scripts against it. A boot script is a text file of
directives (attach an RK05 or TU56 image, type characters at the
console, wait for output, save state, and so on) as used throughout
.IR /usr/share/pidp8i/boot .
It is the driver behind the OS/8 tools in this package: the runtime
disk, the Combined Kit and the game packs are all assembled and
maintained by running scripts of this kind.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h
show the usage message and exit
.TP
.B \-d
debug output
.TP
.B \-v\fR,\ \-vv
progress information on what the script is doing
.TP
.BI \-\-enable " enable_option"
.TQ
.BI \-\-disable " disable_option"
turn individual script features on or off; the usage message lists the
known option names for the scripts given
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
$ cd /usr/share/pidp8i/boot && os8-run add.script
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /var/lib/pidp8i/media/
the images scripts attach to (the guest writes here; group-writable)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR os8-cp (1),
.BR os8pkg (1),
.BR pdp8 (1),
and the OS/8 documentation under
.IR /usr/share/doc/pidp8i/doc/
